      "body": "## Purpose\n\nFixes #45496.\n\nPrevents `moe_wna16_gemm` from reading past the end of `sorted_token_ids` when `num_tokens_post_pad[0]` covers more padded token slots than the allocated sorted-token buffer. The kernel now receives the actual `sorted_token_ids` length, guards both sorted-token reads with that length, and exits early when a block has no valid tokens.\n\n## Test Plan\n\n- Add a CUDA regression that recreates the reported `size_m=17`, `BLOCK_SIZE_M=16`, `sorted_token_ids.shape=[129]`, `num_tokens_post_pad=144` case.\n- Run local whitespace and Python syntax checks.\n\n## Test Result\n\n- `git diff --check` passed.\n- `python.exe -m py_compile tests\\quantization\\test_moe_wna16.py` passed.\n- Not run: `python.exe -m pytest tests\\quantization\\test_moe_wna16.py` because the available local Python runtime does not have `pytest` installed.\n",
